  }), mdx("p", null, "I got two weeks of vacation from the company for my 3-year work anniversary. I decided to finally do something I\u2019d wanted to try for a while: trekking the Haeparang Trail. The Haeparang Trail is a 750km walking route that follows the east coast from Busan all the way up to Goseong in Gangwon-do. I planned to walk Courses 1 through 10 alone, one course per day, over 10 days."), mdx("p", null, "Two full weeks off was\u2026 not ideal. Was it even possible to take 10 business days off? Probably not. This year\u2019s company schedule and the work itself were heavy and dense\u2014every stretch of time felt important to me, and important to the company too. I was convinced there was no way I could carve out two weeks."), mdx("p", null, "And yet, at some point, I picked a time and decided to go. Looking back, there was never going to be a \u201Cgood\u201D time to use this vacation. There wasn\u2019t a season where it felt safe. I just had to use it, and I just had to go."), mdx("p", null, "Because this vacation comes only once every three years, I treated it like I should spend a lot of money and time and go as far as possible and do everything I could. But mentally, I wasn\u2019t doing great. I felt like I\u2019d been force-feeding myself the world\u2019s changes without a break\u2014overstuffed, barely carrying what I could handle, tired, with a folded-up heart collecting small bruises."), mdx("p", null, "I wanted to sort through those things, unfold them, and press them flat. I thought it would be good to talk to no one, hear nothing, see nothing, think a lot, and build a routine completely different from my usual life. So I decided to go to the sea and walk for a long time."), mdx("h1", {
