  }), "\n  "), "\n    ")), mdx("p", null, "From the morning, the Haeparang Trail sent me into the mountains. The markings led straight into endless steep slopes, and I wanted to beg for mercy. Bongdaesan had an incredible number of burial mounds\u2014I figured it must have long been seen as a common burial place for people in nearby villages. It was really hard to tell whether they were actual graves, symbolic mounds, or relocated ones."), mdx("p", null, "Because I was walking every day, recovery after walking became extremely important. After finishing a day\u2019s walk, I tried to avoid walking as much as possible: eat dinner, check into a motel, hand-wash clothes, replenish electrolytes, read a bit, then sleep for 8+ hours. Burning over 1,000 calories a day makes you sensitive to the feeling of stamina being used up and restored. It felt like an RPG character, like there\u2019s a health bar floating above my head\u2014walking drains it, sitting still or eating fills it back up. The sensation becomes vividly physical."), mdx("h1", {
